<title>INDIA: Indian soybean, oil lose on increased arrivals.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean, oil lose on increased arrivals.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices fell on increased arrivals in central Indian on Wednesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Prices fell by 100-150 rupees per tonne on an estimated arrival of 20,000 tonnes, they said.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices rose 300 rupees per tonne on better demand and limited supply. Soymeal and rapeseed extraction were steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal yellow was $275-276 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was $131-132 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,600 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,550-4,575 rupees FOR Bhavnagar. Volume was dull due to limited export demand.</p>
